56 17592186045417 true] [17592186435169 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2u+5v \\\\ u-3v\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+5v \\\\ u-3v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+5v \\\\ u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-3)+0=-2.\n$$" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435170 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435168 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435170 1069 "q-124260" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435170 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435170 1071 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4u+a,\\,y=6u+bv+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435170 1072 #uuid "924019d9-3882-5c74-a8d2-1e7c35a68ea0" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435170 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u \\\\ 6u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u \\\\ 6u+2v-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=4u+0,\\,y=6u+2v+(-1)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+2+(-1)=1.\n$$" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435171 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435167 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435171 1069 "q-124299" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435171 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435171 1071 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=v-7u,\\,y=2v-u\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 \\\\ -1 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435171 1072 #uuid "abc616ba-5b7e-5285-91c7-65fdcb2a91f9" 13194139534756 17592186045417 true] [17592186435171 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}v-7u \\\\ 2v-u\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-7u \\\\ 2v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u+v \\\\ -u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}